.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC
.Dd July 6, 2026
.Dt CLM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clm
.Nd LLM agent with a Lua plugin system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm setup
.Nm
.Op Fl H | Fl -headless
.Op Fl S | Fl -no-stream
.Op Fl V | Fl -version
.Op Fl a Ar name | Fl -agent Ar name
.Op Fl f Ar prompt | Fl -forever Ar prompt
.Op Fl m Ar provider/model-id | Fl -model Ar provider/model-id
.Op Fl -provider Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar prompt | Fl -oneshot Ar prompt
.Op Fl p Ar dir | Fl -plugins Ar dir
.Op Fl r Op Ar id | Fl -resume Op Ar id
.Op Fl u Ar base | Fl -url Ar base
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a conversational LLM agent against any OpenAI-compatible chat
completions endpoint (llama.cpp, Ollama, OpenAI, Anthropic's
OpenAI-compatible endpoint), with a Lua plugin system for custom
tools; see
.Xr clm-tool 5 .
With no options, and when both standard input and standard output are
a terminal,
.Nm
runs its interactive
.Xr curses 3
UI.
Otherwise it falls back to a plain line-oriented REPL on standard
input/output, which is also what
.Fl -oneshot
uses.
.Pp
.Nm Cm setup
writes a starter
.Pa config.lua
and
.Pa secrets.lua
into
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME Ns Pa /clm
(or
.Pa ~/.config/clm
if
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset) and seeds the builtin plugins into its
.Pa plugins
subdirectory; see
.Xr clm-config 5 .
Safe to re-run: it never overwrites a file that already exists.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a Ar name , Fl -agent Ar name
Use the agent profile named
.Ar name
.Po
.Pa ~/.config/clm/agents/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .lua
.Pc .
If omitted, the
.Va agent
key in
.Pa config.lua
is used, or otherwise the top-level
.Va model
setting applies directly with no named profile.
.It Fl f Ar prompt , Fl -forever Ar prompt
Interactive UI mode only.
Submit
.Ar prompt
immediately, then automatically resubmit it every time a turn
completes with nothing else queued, so the agent keeps going without
a human re-prompting it each turn.
.It Fl H , Fl -headless
Force the plain stdio REPL even when standard input and standard
output are both a terminal.
.It Fl m Ar provider/model-id , Fl -model Ar provider/model-id
A
.Qq Ar provider Ns / Ns Ar model-id
spec, same form and meaning as
.Pa config.lua Ns 's
top-level
.Va model
.Pq Xr clm-config 5 :
.Ar provider
names an entry in
.Va providers
to connect through, and
.Ar model-id
is the literal wire model id requested (also the key into that
provider's
.Va models
subtable, if it has a matching override entry there).
A bare
.Ar model-id
with no
.Qq /
is instead used directly as a literal model id to request from
.Fl -url
(or whatever connection is otherwise active), with no provider lookup
and no per-model overrides applied.
Overrides whatever the active agent profile or
.Pa config.lua Ns 's
top-level
.Va model
would otherwise supply.
.It Fl -provider Ar name
Name of an entry in
.Pa config.lua Ns 's
.Va providers
table
.Pq Xr clm-config 5 ,
overriding which provider connection (endpoint, key, wire dialect)
backs the selected model, independent of
.Fl m .
Useful for failing over to a backup endpoint for the current model.
.It Fl o Ar prompt , Fl -oneshot Ar prompt
Run a single prompt headlessly and exit, printing only the assistant's
reply (plus any tool-call/error lines) to standard output.
The process exits 0 if the turn completed successfully, or 1 otherwise.
.It Fl p Ar dir , Fl -plugins Ar dir
Load Lua plugins from
.Ar dir
instead of the default
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME Ns Pa /clm/plugins .
.It Fl r Op Ar id , Fl -resume Op Ar id
Resume the saved session
.Ar id
in the interactive UI, replaying its transcript and continuing the
conversation in the same session log.
.Ar id
may be any unambiguous part of a session id, such as the eight-character
short id shown in the status bar and by the
.Ic /session
command.
With no
.Ar id ,
present a numbered list of saved sessions to pick from.
Sessions are logged automatically to
.Ev XDG_STATE_HOME Ns Pa /clm
.Po default
.Pa ~/.local/state/clm
.Pc ,
one
.Pa .jsonl
file per session, appended to as the conversation goes; on exit the
session id is printed for later resumption, and a session in which
nothing was said is deleted.
A compaction rewrites the file to match the shortened history, so a
resumed session starts compacted rather than replaying what was folded
away; the pre-compaction contents stay beside it as
.Pa .bak
until the next compaction.
Logs untouched for longer than
.Va session_keep_days
.Pq default 90
are deleted when a new session starts, see
.Xr clm-config 5 .
.Pp
Each session also gets a private scratch directory under
.Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME Ns Pa /clm/scratch
.Po default
.Pa ~/.cache/clm/scratch
.Pc ,
named after the session and exported to tools as
.Ev CLM_SCRATCH .
The system prompt points the model at it, so working files land there
instead of in the user's tree.
The cache dir rather than
.Pa /tmp
because /tmp is a memory filesystem on many machines.
Directories whose session log is gone are removed when a new session
starts, subject to the same retention window.
The
.Ic /clear
command starts a fresh session file, leaving the old one resumable.
Incompatible with
.Fl -oneshot
and
.Fl -headless .
.It Fl -allow-all-tools
Run every tool call without asking.
The permission gate exists because a model can be talked into running
something you would not have approved, so this is for an agent nobody is
watching, in a directory whose contents you can afford to lose.
The status bar carries
.Sy [allow-all]
for as long as the session runs this way.
.Fl -oneshot
and
.Fl -headless
runs already allow every call, with or without this flag.
.It Fl S , Fl -no-stream
Request non-streamed responses instead of the default
server-sent-events streaming.
.It Fl u Ar base , Fl -url Ar base
Base API endpoint.
.Pa /chat/completions
is appended automatically; do not include it in
.Ar base .
Defaults to
.Pa http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1 .
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version number and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CLM_API_KEY
Bearer token sent as
.Li Authorization: Bearer Ar key
on every request to the configured endpoint.
Takes precedence over any
.Va api_key
set in
.Pa config.lua
or an agent profile.
Servers that need no authentication (most local llama.cpp/Ollama
setups) can leave this unset.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for
.Pa clm/config.lua ,
.Pa clm/secrets.lua ,
.Pa clm/plugins/ ,
and
.Pa clm/agents/ .
Defaults to
.Pa ~/.config
if unset.
.It Ev CLM_DEBUG_LOG
Path to a file that internal debug logging is appended to.
Unset (the default) disables logging entirely, nothing is written,
and the check is cheap enough to leave alone in production.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/clm/config.lua
Provider, model, agent, and per-tool plugin configuration; see
.Xr clm-config 5 .
.It Pa ~/.config/clm/secrets.lua
API keys and other secrets, kept separate from
.Pa config.lua
so the latter can be shared or checked into dotfiles.
Mode 0600;
.Nm
warns (via
.Ev CLM_DEBUG_LOG )
if it is readable by group or other.
.It Pa ~/.config/clm/agents/*.lua
Per-agent profiles, each overriding or extending
.Pa config.lua Ns 's
settings; see
.Xr clm-config 5 .
.It Pa ~/.config/clm/plugins/*.lua
Lua plugins, each registering one or more tools; see
.Xr clm-tool 5 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Under
.Fl -oneshot ,
the exit status instead reflects whether that single turn completed
successfully (0) or not (1).
.Sh RATE LIMITS
A backend that answers with a rate limit is not a failed turn: the wait
is served and the same request is sent again, up to five times, honouring
the delay the server names in its reply and capping any single wait at a
minute.
The status line shows the same waiting state the outgoing token bucket
uses.
Whether a request is admitted depends on the tokens it carries, not on
the size of the reply it is allowed to generate, so trimming what the
conversation carries -- see
.Va autocompact_tokens
and
.Va volatile_tools
in
.Xr clm-config 5 
-- is what buys throughput.
.Sh CONVERSATION STATE
Every request carries the whole conversation: these APIs keep no session,
so the transcript is the state.
Against an
.Qq openai-responses
provider clm continues the server's own chain instead, sending only the
new turn and pointing at the previous response, which cuts the request
body without changing what the model processes or what it costs.
The chain is abandoned whenever the history stops being an append-only
extension of what the server holds
.Pq compaction, superseded tool results, Ic /clear , No a provider switch ,
and the next request carries everything again.
.Sh AGENT MESSAGING
Each interactive session binds a unix socket named after its session id
under
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR Ns Pa /clm
.Pq or Pa /tmp/clm-<uid> No where that is unset ,
alongside a
.Pa .json
file describing the session.
Other clm instances running as the same user find it by reading that
directory: the
.Sy agents_list
tool reports who is running, and
.Sy agent_send
delivers a line of text to one of them.
.Pp
A headless or
.Fl -oneshot
run gets the same two tools but binds no socket of its own: it can find
and message the agents that are running, and exits too quickly to be
worth answering.
.Pp
A delivered message arrives between the receiving agent's turns, the same
way typed input does, and appears in its transcript marked as coming from
a peer.
It carries text only: a peer cannot make another agent run anything, and
the receiving model decides whether to answer.
Delivery is rate limited per sender, so two agents answering each other
cannot bill forever.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clm_agent 3 ,
.Xr clm-config 5 ,
.Xr clm-tool 5
